+	 * ioremap() on ARM means MT_DEVICE -- Device memory -- while simplefb
+	 * maps the very same physical VRAM pages with ioremap_wc(), i.e.
+	 * Normal non-cacheable. Two live mappings of one physical address with
+	 * different memory types is architecturally UNPREDICTABLE on ARMv6
+	 * (ARM ARM, "Mismatched memory attributes"), and the permitted
+	 * behaviours explicitly include loss of coherency *and unexpected
+	 * aborts*. That matters here because an external abort on a bufferable
+	 * write is imprecise on ARM11: it is not reported at the offending
+	 * store, it is reported at the next barrier that drains the write
+	 * buffer -- and the barriers this kernel hits constantly are the
